### Verification method to resume once the weights are available

For invertible shape matrices B_q, use C_q = {c_q + B_q z : ‖z‖₂ ≤ r_q}. A full ambient ellipsoid avoids silently
discarding the radial contribution of a curved sphere. Candidate shapes may be fitted from the block Jacobians;
their numerical construction is exploratory and must be verified separately.

For every admissible word w of length k from q to t, enclose

    b_qw = ‖B_t⁻¹(F_w(c_q) − c_t)‖₂,
    γ_qw ≥ sup_{h ∈ C_q} ‖B_t⁻¹ D F_w(h) B_q‖₂.

The mean-value theorem on the convex source ellipsoid gives the sufficient containment inequality
`b_qw + γ_qw r_q ≤ r_t`. The derivative enclosure must follow the actual composed map through all ticks,
including normalization; multiplying Jacobians at independently recentered states is only a linearised diagnostic.
For every proper prefix, bound every correct-minus-competing logit from below over its image and require strict
positivity. Include the empty prefix (boundary readout), all applicable paths, and initial-state inclusion or all
exact-prefix entry paths. Search k=1…6 and radii only after these quantities can be evaluated from the weights.

Floating-point soundness is still an implementation obligation: fixed weight bits must define the target map, and
centre evaluation, matrix products, inverse/norm bounds, nonlinear functions, and all comparisons need outward
enclosures or proved error allowances. If certifying the executed floating-point recurrence rather than its real
arithmetic interpretation, enclose its per-step evaluation errors too. Float64 replay alone is not exact arithmetic.
In particular, the legacy `cert_sound.py` uses ordinary NumPy/JAX arithmetic and derivative grids with a safety factor;
those files alone do not supply the explicit rounding proof required by this registration. Their values above remain
prior diagnostics, not a new sound certificate.

The immediate requirement is recovery of the fixed weights into this worktree (plus the old sampling data if reusing
the exact old centres). After recovery, the search must measure whether anisotropic shapes reduce the residual and
readout gap and whether certified nonlinear bounds remain useful at the required radii. No such improvement is
established by this audit.

