The first completed Lean result exposes a weakness in the bound: at k=6, the verified centre Jacobian norm is about 0.006, but multiplying sublayer error bounds loses that contraction. I’m tightening how errors propagate across event boundaries before continuing the full run, so the KILL gap is more informative.

