### Reproduction, inputs, and implementation checks

The recovered inventory is "'`results/recovered_inputs.json`: 269 NPZ files, 2,317,998,115 bytes, including all 30
registered weight files. Each used checkpoint and its training metadata has a SHA-256 digest. The original worktree
was read in place; the ignored `.local/unify` link is the only connection to it. Fresh deterministic centres remove
the dependency on the old `m2k.npz` sampling archive. There was no retraining, weight replacement, or source-worktree
modification.

With the ignored link present, reproduce the search from the repository root:

```sh
research/cert/run_search.sh
nice -n 19 python3 research/cert/summarize.py
nice -n 19 python3 -u research/cert/audit_recovered.py --require-results
```

If needed, first create `research/cert/.local` and link its `unify` entry to
`/Users/neo/repos/polyformer/.claude/worktrees/unify-85e792/research/unify`. `run_search.sh` pins the Python dependencies,
forces JAX to CPU, applies nice 19, and emits unbuffered progress plus a 20-second heartbeat. It also supports
`--kind lean|s5 --seeds ...` for disjoint CPU batches, and `--resume` for already completed per-checkpoint JSON files.
The per-checkpoint JSONs retain selected centre coordinates, valid event words, bound coefficients, readout caps,
monotone radius iterations, and the accepted/rejected radius brackets. `results/environment.json` records versions,
precision, CPU device, niceness, and verifier source hashes. `summarize.py` refuses an incomplete 30-checkpoint,
540-candidate result set and checks every rejection and bracket before producing the summary.

`check_verifier.py` independently compares both adapters with the original checkpoint recurrence, compares the Arb
two-event map and analytic Jacobian with JAX replay/autodiff, checks a non-normal matrix'"'s spectral-norm enclosure,
and checks random perturbation remainders at three radii. Both models passed; logs are "'`results/qa_lean.txt` and
`results/qa_s5.txt`. These finite comparisons are implementation QA, not all-length correctness evidence. Early
implementation probes caught inadequate interval precision and a zero-crossing interval-power issue; both were
fixed before the final search, and non-finite balls now abort rather than enter a numerical result.
