# CERT: block certificate for a trained group tracker

## Final verdict (29 October 2026): KILL

**The registered CPU search finished: all 10 Lean AIM+N and all 20 S5 AIM+Nc checkpoints reject for every
k = 1…6 and all three tested Jacobian-derived shapes: 540/540 candidate sufficient systems are infeasible.**
No complete certificate was found. The largest certified invariant radius is **none** (recorded as 0 in the
machine summary; a zero-radius certificate was not established either). This is a KILL of the specified search,
not a proof that no other centres, ellipsoids, multinorms, readout bounds, or nonlinear verifier could succeed.

The weights were present in the original UNIFY worktree, as the user reported. All 30 checkpoint hashes match
before/after computation. Missing inputs no longer block the task. All numerical runs used CPU at nice 19, with
progress output; remote compute spend was **$0**. No training, GPU, push, or modification of the source worktree occurred.

### Numbers

The table selects the smallest direct radius contradiction for each k over the tested seeds/shapes. Within a
candidate, the worse selected state determines the gap. `r_need` is the radius forced by an incoming centre
residual in the sufficient containment system. `r_allow` is the upper bracket on the largest source radius this
verifier can admit even when the target is enlarged to its sufficient readout cap. These are **local rejection
diagnostics, not certified invariant radii**. The full result files include both bracket endpoints.

Shape exponent alpha denotes `B = (I + J_word^T J_word)^alpha`, rescaled to maximum semiaxis one;
alpha = 0 is the Euclidean ball. Radii are in the selected ellipsoid coordinates. The reported cell cap belongs
to the witness target state; it is not a minimum over all automaton states or the exact decoding-boundary distance.

#### Lean AIM+N (10 checkpoints)

| k | Seed / alpha | r_need | r_allow | Target cell cap | Gap (approx.) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 4 / 0 | 0.44563 | 0.00336964 | 1.45247 | 132.249× |
| 2 | 4 / -0.5 | 0.470128 | 0.000722795 | 1.35326 | 650.43× |
| 3 | 4 / -0.5 | 0.476866 | 0.000336013 | 1.45247 | 1419.19× |
| 4 | 4 / -0.5 | 0.477068 | 0.000193897 | 1.35326 | 2460.41× |
| 5 | 4 / -0.5 | 0.477301 | 0.000135347 | 1.45247 | 3526.51× |
| 6 | 4 / -0.5 | 0.477248 | 9.87188e-05 | 1.35326 | 4834.42× |

#### S5 AIM+Nc (20 checkpoints)

| k | Seed / alpha | r_need | r_allow | Target cell cap | Gap (approx.) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | 0 / 0 | 0.540392 | 0.0883697 | 2.41964 | 6.11512× |
| 2 | 0 / 0 | 0.890077 | 0.0245838 | 2.41964 | 36.2058× |
| 3 | 0 / 0 | 1.10575 | 0.0117772 | 2.41964 | 93.8894× |
| 4 | 6 / -0.5 | 1.1426 | 0.00675406 | 2.08604 | 169.173× |
| 5 | 6 / -0.5 | 1.16913 | 0.00459839 | 2.08604 | 254.247× |
| 6 | 6 / -0.5 | 1.18059 | 0.00340706 | 2.08604 | 346.514× |

The tightest direct contradiction is S5 seed 0, k=1: the observed one-event centre miss is
0.540391650 raw units, the witness readout cap is 2.419642706, but the
admitted input radius is only 0.088369703 (gap about 6.115124×). Its raw two-event return
miss is 0.890077194. Lean's smallest direct gap is about 132.248614× (seed 4,
k=1); the witness's raw two-event return miss is 0.468559454.

**The smallest direct-gap cases already fail the relaxed linearised test.** They are not the closest complete
certificates. Of the 180 Lean and 360 S5 candidates, respectively, 135 and 4 pass the selected-path linearised
relaxation, and every one fails once the verified nonlinear remainder is included. Among those linear survivors,
the smallest direct gaps are **650.430×** for Lean seed 4, k=2, alpha=-0.5,
and **254.247×** for S5 seed 6, k=5, alpha=-0.5. These remain subset diagnostics.

Float64 readout of the fitted centres reports zero errors over all 960 Lean states and all 120 S5 states for
every seed; the selected witnesses also have positive margins enclosed independently in Arb. The reported
obstruction is therefore not a misdecoded witness centre. Strong pointwise block contraction also survives: for example, Lean seed 0
has a verified full-ambient six-event Jacobian norm below 0.005990 on one selected return path, while its centre
landing miss is about 0.6682. The nonlinear enclosure still cannot absorb that miss within the readout cap.

### What would close the gap

At minimum, the chosen centres/shapes/bounds must resolve the direct radius contradictions above. Clearing the
6.115× S5 contradiction alone would not suffice: that candidate also needs a better centre/metric or sharper
containment estimate to clear its linearised obstruction. Even the S5 candidate that clears the linearised
relaxation needs the admitted radius to increase by at least 254.2×, or a commensurate reduction in
the forced residual, before this particular local obstruction disappears. Those factors concern the verifier
inequalities, not a lower bound on improvements required by an optimal nonlinear certificate.

The plausible next changes are centre optimisation against worst return-word residuals; stronger state-dependent
multinorm fitting; and local, directional nonlinear bounds (for example CROWN or tighter Taylor models retaining
suffix-Jacobian cancellation of individual remainder terms). This run used global GELU derivative constants,
Euclidean remainder balls, event-level remainder propagation, and a ball-based sufficient readout cap. Those
choices remain conservative; CROWN/alpha-CROWN and general multinorm optimisation were not run.

Any survivor would still have to satisfy every state, every admissible word, every intermediate prefix, and
direct or exact-prefix entry. None survived even the relaxed return-path subsystem, so universal enumeration
and entry/prefix checking were unnecessary for this negative verdict. In particular, the valid S5 identity-event
witnesses suffice to reject a candidate but do not replace the full distractor/placement alphabet for a PASS.

The numerical evidence is in `results/summary.json`, `results/lean_*.json`, and `results/s5_*.json`; the soundness
argument, exact search scope, input provenance, and reproduction commands follow the historical audit below.

---
## Registration (29 October 2026, before certificate computation)

All runs are CPU-only. The trained checkpoints are fixed: first the Lean AIM+N trackers from
`research/unify/lean/results/unify_lean`, then the S5 AIM+Nc trackers from
`research/unify/s5/results/unify_s5`.

For each block length \(k=1,\ldots,6\), the search will use one ellipsoidal neighbourhood \(C_q\) per automaton state \(q\),
shaped from the trained tracker's block Jacobians or a state-dependent multinorm. A candidate is a certificate only if sound
bounds establish all of the following:

1. the trained initial hidden state belongs to \(C_{q_0}\), or the exact-prefix entry condition of Theorem U10″ is checked;
2. for every state \(q\) and every word \(w\) of length \(k\),
   \(f_w(C_q)\subseteq C_{\delta(q,w)}\);
3. for every state \(q\), every such word, and every proper prefix \(u\) of \(w\),
   \(f_u(C_q)\) is contained in the readout cell for \(\delta(q,u)\);
4. each boundary set \(C_q\) is contained in the readout cell for \(q\).

The nonlinear image bounds must cover the entire ellipsoid, not samples or centre Jacobians alone. Any floating-point
roundoff used in a positive result must be enclosed explicitly (directed interval rounding or a conservative analytic error
allowance).

**Pass.** At least one fixed, trained tracker on a non-absorbing automaton has a complete certificate satisfying every
condition above for some \(k\leq 6\).

**Kill.** No tested Lean or S5 AIM tracker closes for any \(k\leq 6\). The report will state the tightest sound gap, the
largest certified radius, the observed centre/landing miss, the limiting readout-cell radius, and what improvement would close
the gap.

The final report will distinguish exploratory/linearised evidence from sound certification and will not count finite rollout
tests as a certificate.

## Historical takeover audit (29 October 2026; superseded)

**Historical status at commit 7fa0411c: blocked on missing inputs; neither PASS nor KILL.** The registered ellipsoid search has not run.
There is no newly established certified radius; reporting zero would incorrectly suggest a completed search.
